# 9. SIMULTANEOUS ROUND SYSTEM

IMPORTANT: This game must use SIMULTANEOUS ROUNDS, not sequential turn-by-turn play.

All players participate in each round at the same time.

Round flow:

STEP 1 — ROUND START

- Teacher starts the round.
- The system creates a round number.
- All active players receive the round state.

STEP 2 — DICE ROLL

Each player rolls a virtual dice.

Dice result is a random integer from 1 to 6.

Dice results should be generated and validated by the trusted server or server-side logic.

Do not allow students to manipulate dice results from client-side code.

STEP 3 — QUESTION

Each player receives a mathematics question.

Questions may differ between players but must have equivalent difficulty.

Display:

- Current round
- Dice result
- Mathematics question
- Answer input
- Countdown timer

STEP 4 — ANSWER

Students submit answers.

Each player can submit only one answer per round unless the teacher explicitly enables retry mode.

Record:

- Player ID
- Round ID
- Question
- Correct answer
- Submitted answer
- Correct/incorrect status
- Response time
- Timestamp

STEP 5 — ROUND DEADLINE

When the timer expires:

- Players who answered are processed.
- Players who did not answer are marked TIMEOUT.
- No further answers are accepted.
- Resolve all movements.

STEP 6 — MOVEMENT

Correct answer:

- Move forward according to dice result.

Incorrect answer:

- Apply teacher-configured penalty.

Timeout:

- Default: stay in place.

STEP 7 — BOARD EFFECTS

After normal movement:

- Process ladder
- Process snake
- Process bonus tile
- Process challenge tile

STEP 8 — ROUND SUMMARY

Show:

- Correct answers
- Incorrect answers
- Timeout
- Players who moved
- Players who climbed ladders
- Players who slid down snakes
- Players who reached finish

STEP 9 — NEXT ROUND

Automatically transition to the next round when the round summary is completed.

The teacher may also have a setting:

- Automatic next round
- Teacher-controlled next round

Default: Automatic next round after a short summary.

All clients must remain synchronized.

